@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Research
+
+## Request paths and causes
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java`
+  exposes `POST /api/v1/cart` and `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}` without consulting the request principal. Both call the legacy anonymous facade methods, so the cart created by an authenticated customer has a null `customerId`, and an authenticated customer can modify a cart without ownership enforcement.
+- The authenticated `GET /api/v1/auth/customer/cart` endpoint delegates to `shoppingCartFacadev1.get`. `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` always loads the customer's first open cart when no code is supplied, and when a code is supplied it calls `mergeCart` rather than validating that the cart belongs to the customer. `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getShoppingCart` also takes the first result from `findByCustomer` without a deterministic recency ordering.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartRepository.java` has only an unordered `findByCustomer` query. The cart model has `customerId` and `orderId`; `orderId == null` is the open/current-cart condition used by the service.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderTotalApi.java` correctly attempts to check the authenticated customer and cart `customerId`, but wraps the entire operation in a catch that sends HTTP 503 for every exception. It calculates through `orderService.caculateOrderTotal(orderSummary, customer, merchantStore, language)`, which is the same customer-aware calculation used by checkout and therefore the right route for delivery-address tax.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` authenticated checkout loads a cart by code without checking its `customerId`, then wraps all failures—including `ConversionException` from payment amount mismatch—in HTTP 503. `OrderFacadeImpl.processOrder` calculates the order total with the authenticated customer, compares the submitted payment amount, and only sets `cart.orderId` after `orderService.processOrder`, so a rejected amount should not create an order or consume the cart.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` builds authenticated order criteria with `customerId`, but `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java` routes it through `listOrders`, which is the admin/store listing query and does not apply `customerId`. The separate `listByStore` query applies `customerId`, orders by `o.id desc`, and returns the count, but does not set total pages. `EntityList.getTotalPages()` defaults zero to one, so page metadata is wrong for customer lists.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/OrderCriteria.java` carries customer id and page start/count; `ReadableOrderList` exposes `recordsTotal` and `totalPages`.
+
+## Affected behavior
+
+The changes must preserve anonymous cart behavior, prevent cross-customer cart reads/modifications/totals/checkout, make the no-parameter customer cart deterministic and open-cart-only, preserve customer-aware tax calculation, return a client error containing the calculated amount for payment mismatches, mark carts checked out only after successful order processing, and populate customer order count/page metadata while retaining newest-first ordering.
+
